[WORK]
UID: WORK-AUTHORSHIP-IDENTITY
TITLE: Authorship identity: keys for the LLM and how AUTHORED_BY gets set
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The umbrella node for giving the LLM its own signing identity and for making
authorship attach to a write automatically from that identity. Two children
hang off it: WORK-LLM-SIGNING-KEYS, provisioning SSH and GPG keys for the LLM
in SecretSpec, and WORK-ASSESS-AUTO-AUTHORSHIP, assessing how a key turns into
recorded authorship at write time.

This does not reopen DEC-AUTHORSHIP-LADDER, the accepted decision that
AUTHORED_BY is one monotonic field (llm / llm-accepted / llm-adopted / human)
governing reversal rather than credit, nor MECH-RUNTIME-WRITE-GUARD, which
already keeps AUTHORED_BY and PARENT_FP out of the writer's hands by giving the
CLI no flag for either and writing llm unconditionally on create. What the two
children below are after is upstream of both: a real identity for the writer to
be graded against, and a mechanism that sets the grade from that identity
instead of the current unconditional default.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Operator, 2026-09-02, verbatim: "need new nodes, all related likely under one
